WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.590
Draw a straight line across
China, from Heihe to Tengchong.

2
00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:08.790
The geographer Hu
Huanyong drew it in 1935.

3
00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:14.710
On 1933 data, 96 per cent of China's
people lived south-east of it.

4
00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:18.830
The 2010 census: about 94
per cent of the people,

5
00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:21.570
on about 43 per cent of the land.

6
00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:25.390
In about 90 years, the
split has barely changed.

7
00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:28.510
Why do more than nine
in ten stay on one side?

8
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:33.010
In this mission, you'll sort the physical
and human factors that shape where people

9
00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:34.050
live.

10
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:38.070
Then you'll cross to Egypt, and calculate
how crowded its ribbon of settlement

11
00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:39.130
is.

12
00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:44.250
Your mission: explain why China's population
is concentrated on one side of the

13
00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:45.090
Hu Line.
